{"user": "You mentioned \"stable discs\"... I'm not sure I follow. What does that mean exactly?", "user_ts": "2026-08-10T22:05:45.891334+00:00", "assistant": "\u201cStable discs\u201d are discs that **can never be flipped again**, no matter what happens.\n\nThe easiest example: **corners**. Once a disc is in a corner, it is permanent because it can\u2019t be surrounded from both sides.\n\nThen corners can \u201cprotect\u201d nearby edge discs. For example, if White owns **a1**, then White discs along the top edge like **b1, c1, d1\u2026** may become stable too, because Black can\u2019t get behind them from the corner side.\n\nIn this final board, White has long stable edges from the corners, so many White discs became impossible to flip back. That\u2019s why the score got lopsided.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-10T22:05:45.891334+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-10T22:05:50.891334+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Metacomment": 2}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Metacomment": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Board Report": 1}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Board Report": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min